===Etymology===
From {{etyl|goh|de}} {{m|goh|drīzehan}}, akin to Old Saxon {{m|osx|thriutein}}. Ultimately from {{etyl|gem-pro|de}} {{m|gem-pro|*þritehun}}. Compare Dutch {{m|nl|dertien}}, West Frisian {{m|fy|trettjin}}, English {{m|en|thirteen}}, Danish {{m|da|tretten}}, Gothic [[𐌸𐍂𐌹𐍄𐌰𐌹𐌷𐌿𐌽]] (þritaihun).

